  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Well Production Monitoring for an upstream operator with 20 wells (mostly horizontals plus a few verticals) on 11 multi-well pads across the Wolfcamp, Bone Spring, Spraberry, Eagle Ford, Niobrara, Bakken/Three Forks, Haynesville, Marcellus, Utica, Woodford, SCOOP, and San Andres plays. Stakeholders include Production Engineers (rates, pressure, status, lift efficiency), Field Superintendents (pad-level uptime, deferred barrels), and the Asset Manager (LOE/BOE, water cut, cumulative oil).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Oil rate = oil_bpd; gas rate = gas_mcfpd; water rate = water_bpd.\n- Tubing pressure = tubing_pressure_psi; casing pressure = casing_pressure_psi (flow-assurance signals).\n- Well status = well_status (Flowing / Shut-In / Workover / Completion / Abandoned); only Flowing produces revenue.\n- Water cut = water_cut_pct (weekly snapshot); >60% prioritize water handling, >75% near economic limit.\n- GOR (SCF/BBL) = gor_scf_bbl; rising GOR can indicate gas breakthrough or reservoir-energy decline.\n- Uptime = uptime_pct; target \u226595%, <90% flag for root-cause.\n- Lift efficiency = artificial_lift_efficiency_pct; <70% flags ESP/rod-pump optimization opportunity.\n- Deferred oil = deferred_oil_bbl (BBL not produced due to downtime/chokes).\n- LOE/BOE = loe_per_boe (USD); onshore US benchmark $6-12/BOE.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - production_readings_metrics (source: production_readings) \u2014 dims: reading_date, well_id, well_type, pad_name, well_status; measures: avg_oil_bpd, avg_gas_mcfpd, avg_water_bpd, avg_tubing_pressure, total_casing_pressure_psi, max_oil_bpd.\n  - well_status_snapshots_metrics (source: well_status_snapshots) \u2014 dims: snapshot_date, well_id, well_type, pad_name; measures: avg_water_cut, avg_uptime_pct, avg_lift_efficiency, total_cumulative_oil, total_gor_scf_bbl, max_cumulative_oil_bbl.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. well_name, deferred_oil_bbl, loe_per_boe, monthly_oil_bbl, gor_scf_bbl).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 wells by average oil rate (BOPD) over the last 90 days.",
    "Show the monthly trend in total deferred oil BBL by pad for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which wells have uptime below 90% or lift efficiency below 70%, and what pad are they on?",
    "What is the average LOE per BOE by pad and well type year to date?",
    "Top 10 wells by water cut % \u2014 and how does that compare to last quarter?",
    "How has average GOR trended month over month across horizontal wells?",
    "Which pads have the most shut-in or workover wells right now, and what is the deferred oil impact?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How has average oil barrels per day trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_oil_bpd) AS avg_oil_bpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average gas mcf/day trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_gas_mcfpd) AS avg_gas_mcfpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total gor scf/barrels trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_gor_scf_bbl) AS total_gor_scf_bbl",
        "FROM {fqn}.well_status_snapshots_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which currently-flowing wells are producing the most oil?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT well_name, AVG(oil_bpd) AS avg_oil_bpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.well_production",
        "WHERE well_status = 'Flowing'",
        "GROUP BY well_name",
        "ORDER BY avg_oil_bpd DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total cumulative oil barrels trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(cumulative_oil_bbl) AS total_cumulative_oil_bbl",
        "FROM {fqn}.well_status_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does average daily oil production compare across pads?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT pad_name, AVG(oil_bpd) AS avg_oil_bpd",
        "FROM {fqn}.well_production",
        "GROUP BY pad_name",
        "ORDER BY avg_oil_bpd DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average tubing pressure changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_tubing_pressure) AS avg_tubing_pressure",
        "FROM {fqn}.production_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
